<header class="start-masthead"><p class="eyebrow">Lab runtime · proposed documentation</p><h1>Operate the Lab</h1><p>Choose the implementation and the next task before relying on a runtime result.</p><p class="source-note">Draft prepared on 2026-10-14. Integration and final T21 qualification remain pending.</p></header>

<section id="runtime-overview-start-with-the-admitted-inspection-path" aria-labelledby="runtime-overview-start-with-the-admitted-inspection-path-title"><h2 id="runtime-overview-start-with-the-admitted-inspection-path-title">Start with the admitted inspection path</h2>

<p>For a first inspection, use the admitted local v1 executable and its frozen Decision 0074 source profile. Decision 0075 admits that exact executable for local inspection, authorized local transactions, replay/recovery and ephemeral context. The admission is an external overlay: its original README can still say candidate without undoing the later decision. Read the <a href="research/sources/implementation/lab-runtime/ADMISSION.md">admission scope</a>, then follow <a href="runtime-first-inspection.html">first inspection</a>.</p>

<p>The three-command walkthrough checks public source files and selects a deliberately nonexistent store. It creates no store, key or transaction. Its observed output is D74 with 698 verified sources and 468 subjects. This is a useful working entrypoint; it is separate from a permanent service, a new installation and the expanded API.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-overview-choose-a-surface" aria-labelledby="runtime-overview-choose-a-surface-title"><h2 id="runtime-overview-choose-a-surface-title">Choose a surface</h2>

<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Surface</th><th scope="col">What you can rely on</th><th scope="col">What remains separate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Admitted runtime v1</td><td>Exact local executable admitted by D75, reading its D74 profile</td><td>Current repository D75, permanent service and external consumers</td></tr><tr><td>Runtime v2</td><td>Separate D75 source-profile candidate</td><td>Its candidate review does not replace v1 admission</td></tr><tr><td>API16 / composite catalog</td><td>Code and declared contracts for 28 Base, 3 Action and 3 Governance operations</td><td>Full current three-branch qualification and actual permission</td></tr><tr><td>Changed API17</td><td>Reviewed overlay code exists</td><td>Old e417/5c capture is ineligible after changes; new family/selector/capture work is incomplete</td></tr><tr><td>Paperclip 2026.1005.0</td><td>Recorded bounded process-reader episode</td><td>Live availability, a fresh grant, autonomous Work and human usefulness</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<p>These surfaces have different stores, channels and evidence. A filename, result envelope or catalog count cannot select an authority boundary for you. The <a href="runtime-status.html">dated status page</a> identifies the evidence cut.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-overview-choose-your-next-task" aria-labelledby="runtime-overview-choose-your-next-task-title"><h2 id="runtime-overview-choose-your-next-task-title">Choose your next task</h2>

<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Your task</th><th scope="col">Reading route</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Inspect a public record and explain its standing</td><td><a href="runtime-first-inspection.html">First inspection</a></td></tr><tr><td>Prepare a disposable local Work proposal</td><td><a href="runtime-local-work.html">Local Work</a> and <a href="runtime-provision.html">provision and review</a></td></tr><tr><td>Understand agents and their limits</td><td><a href="runtime-sessions.html">Agent sessions</a></td></tr><tr><td>Deal with a timeout or pending effect</td><td><a href="runtime-recovery.html">Recover and retry</a></td></tr><tr><td>Connect Paperclip to a selected reader</td><td><a href="runtime-paperclip.html">Paperclip</a></td></tr><tr><td>Export, import or install a package</td><td><a href="runtime-packages.html">Packages and installation</a></td></tr><tr><td>Trace the code and state ownership</td><td><a href="runtime-architecture.html">Architecture</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<p>For meanings, use the existing <a href="governance-lab-reference.html#records">record and definition library</a> rather than treating these operational pages as replacement definitions.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-overview-what-a-result-establishes" aria-labelledby="runtime-overview-what-a-result-establishes-title"><h2 id="runtime-overview-what-a-result-establishes-title">What a result establishes</h2>

<p>Record the selected executable/profile, source cut, current permission, exact input and observed output. Then read the result posture. A prepared candidate, an admitted record, an actual action and an assessed benefit are distinct facts.</p>

<p>The full integrated learning path is not yet a supported successful tutorial. The measured episode expired, and the later family4 build exposed a dependency cycle before final runtime qualification. Those failures remain in <a href="runtime-status.html">status</a> and <a href="runtime-maintenance.html">maintenance</a>. This handbook preparation does not close T21 or publish a release.</p>

</section>

